                <pb facs="0139" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg35"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Mizner</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 21,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Adee informs Mr. Mizner of the report by the president of the Pacific Mail
                    Company of the seizure by Guatemala of the Company’s steam launch used at San
                    José for the transfer of passengers, and adds that sufficient instructions have
                    been already sent to Mr. Mizner.</p>
            </div>
